    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 3\n    Q = 53  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[67, 53], [10, 26], [9, 72], [94, 10], [89, 10]]\n    demands = [17, 19, 24, 25, 22]\n    time_windows = [[0, 349], [20, 85], [43, 98], [70, 125], [83, 179], [58, 124]]\n    service_times = [5, 8, 10, 11, 6]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Subject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Time-Windowed Deliveries\n\nOverview\nWe operate a small fleet of identical vehicles from a single central depot to complete a set of customer deliveries within a single planning horizon. Each customer has a defined delivery window and a required unloading time. Our task is to design efficient routes and schedules that honor these commitments while making effective use of our fleet.\n\nDelivery Challenge\n- All vehicles depart the depot at time 0.\n- Each vehicle performs a single continuous trip: depart at time 0, visit an ordered sequence of customers, and return to the depot before the end-of-day cutoff specified for the depot.\n- Every customer must be visited exactly once. No split deliveries or repeat visits.\n- Vehicles are identical in capacity and operating characteristics. Deploying a vehicle incurs a fixed cost, and travel adds distance-related cost.\n\nOperating Rules and Requirements\n- Time windows: Delivery at a customer must start within the customer\u2019s specified time window. If a vehicle arrives early, it waits until the window opens. Service begins at the start of the window (if waiting) or upon arrival (if within the window).\n- Service times: Each stop requires a defined unloading/service duration. Departure from the stop occurs at arrival_time + service_time, or window_open + service_time when waiting is required.\n- Capacity: Each customer has a known demand that consumes capacity on the assigned vehicle. The total demand on any route must not exceed the vehicle\u2019s capacity at any point.\n- Depot return: All vehicles must return to the depot before the depot\u2019s latest allowable time.\n- Travel time and distance: Travel time between any two locations is taken as the straight-line distance between their coordinates, with a unit speed assumption (one unit of distance equals one unit of time).\n- Cost structure: Using each vehicle adds a fixed deployment cost on top of the total travel distance cost, creating a tradeoff between deploying more vehicles and driving longer routes.\n\nPlanning Goal\nIdentify a set of routes and schedules\u2014one for each deployed vehicle\u2014that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Respect all customer time windows and service times,\n- Stay within vehicle capacity at all times,\n- Ensure each vehicle returns to the depot before the depot\u2019s closing time, and\n- Minimize the sum of total travel distance and the fixed deployment costs of the vehicles used.\n\nExpected Outputs\nFor each deployed vehicle, provide the customer visit sequence, planned arrival and departure times at each stop (accounting for any waiting), confirmation of capacity feasibility along the route, and the planned return time to the depot. Also report the total travel distance and the total cost including fixed deployment charges.\n\nANNEX \u2014 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): (50, 50)\n- Depot closing time: 349\n- Customer locations (coordinates): Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (67, 53)\n  - C2: (10, 26)\n  - C3: (9, 72)\n  - C4: (94, 10)\n  - C5: (89, 10)\n- Customer delivery demands (units): Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 17 units\n  - C2: 19 units\n  - C3: 24 units\n  - C4: 25 units\n  - C5: 22 units\n- Customer time windows (earliest, latest): Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [20, 85]\n  - C2: [43, 98]\n  - C3: [70, 125]\n  - C4: [83, 179]\n  - C5: [58, 124]\n- Customer service times (per stop): Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 5\n  - C2: 8\n  - C3: 10\n  - C4: 11\n  - C5: 6\n- Vehicle capacity (units): 53\n- Number of available vehicles: 3\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: 100.0",
    "LLM_description_template": "Subject: Routing and Scheduling Plan for Time-Windowed Deliveries\n\nOverview\nWe operate a small fleet of identical vehicles from a single central depot to complete a set of customer deliveries within a single planning horizon. Each customer has a defined delivery window and a required unloading time. Our task is to design efficient routes and schedules that honor these commitments while making effective use of our fleet.\n\nDelivery Challenge\n- All vehicles depart the depot at time 0.\n- Each vehicle performs a single continuous trip: depart at time 0, visit an ordered sequence of customers, and return to the depot before the end-of-day cutoff specified for the depot.\n- Every customer must be visited exactly once. No split deliveries or repeat visits.\n- Vehicles are identical in capacity and operating characteristics. Deploying a vehicle incurs a fixed cost, and travel adds distance-related cost.\n\nOperating Rules and Requirements\n- Time windows: Delivery at a customer must start within the customer\u2019s specified time window. If a vehicle arrives early, it waits until the window opens. Service begins at the start of the window (if waiting) or upon arrival (if within the window).\n- Service times: Each stop requires a defined unloading/service duration. Departure from the stop occurs at arrival_time + service_time, or window_open + service_time when waiting is required.\n- Capacity: Each customer has a known demand that consumes capacity on the assigned vehicle. The total demand on any route must not exceed the vehicle\u2019s capacity at any point.\n- Depot return: All vehicles must return to the depot before the depot\u2019s latest allowable time.\n- Travel time and distance: Travel time between any two locations is taken as the straight-line distance between their coordinates, with a unit speed assumption (one unit of distance equals one unit of time).\n- Cost structure: Using each vehicle adds a fixed deployment cost on top of the total travel distance cost, creating a tradeoff between deploying more vehicles and driving longer routes.\n\nPlanning Goal\nIdentify a set of routes and schedules\u2014one for each deployed vehicle\u2014that:\n- Visit every customer exactly once,\n- Respect all customer time windows and service times,\n- Stay within vehicle capacity at all times,\n- Ensure each vehicle returns to the depot before the depot\u2019s closing time, and\n- Minimize the sum of total travel distance and the fixed deployment costs of the vehicles used.\n\nExpected Outputs\nFor each deployed vehicle, provide the customer visit sequence, planned arrival and departure times at each stop (accounting for any waiting), confirmation of capacity feasibility along the route, and the planned return time to the depot. Also report the total travel distance and the total cost including fixed deployment charges.\n\nANNEX \u2014 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): {DEPOT_LOCATION}\n- Depot closing time: {DEPOT_CLOSING_TIME}\n- Customer locations (coordinates): {CUSTOMER_LOCATIONS}\n- Customer delivery demands (units): {CUSTOMER_DEMANDS}\n- Customer time windows (earliest, latest): {TIME_WINDOWS}\n- Customer service times (per stop): {SERVICE_TIMES}\n- Vehicle capacity (units): {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}\n- Number of available vehicles: {NUM_VEHICLES}\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: {VEHICLE_FIXED_COST}"
